/**
 * @defgroup RoModular_Governance_AIAgents_Workspace Workspace Bootstrap
 * @ingroup RoModular_Governance_AIAgents
 * @brief Clone the ecosystem and configure a shared Codex or Claude workspace.
 *
 * @section RoModularWorkspaceBootstrapPurpose Purpose
 *
 * RoModular provides equivalent shell and PowerShell entry points for creating
 * the complete multi-repository workspace:
 *
 * - `scripts/bootstrap-workspace.sh` for macOS and other POSIX environments.
 * - `scripts/bootstrap-workspace.ps1` for Windows PowerShell.
 *
 * Both scripts consume the same repository manifest and install the same
 * workspace-level Codex and Claude adapters. Platform wrappers contain only
 * the behavior required by their native shell.
 *
 * @section RoModularWorkspaceBootstrapContents Repositories
 *
 * The checked-in `.romodular/workspace/repositories.txt` manifest currently
 * defines these local directories:
 *
 * | Directory | Repository |
 * | --------- | ---------- |
 * | `RoModular` | Ecosystem portal and governance |
 * | `RoModularAgents` | Provider-neutral agent contracts, adapters, and skills |
 * | `RoModularBuild` | Shared build infrastructure |
 * | `CPSTL` | Cross-platform STL for hosted and freestanding C++ |
 * | `Foundation` | Low-level C++ library |
 * | `DspCore` | Signal-processing library |
 * | `MCC` | Music Composition Core |
 * | `MIDILAR` | MIDI protocol, translation and devices |
 *
 * Directory names are independent from remote repository names. For example,
 * the `MCC` directory clones the `MusicCompositionCore` repository.
 *
 * @section RoModularWorkspaceBootstrapUsage Usage
 *
 * By default, a standalone checkout creates a sibling directory named
 * `RoModularWorkspace`. When the active RoModular checkout is already inside
 * an initialized workspace, the script reuses that parent directory. The
 * destination remains configurable with `--root`, `-Root`, or the
 * `ROMODULAR_WORKSPACE_ROOT` environment variable.
 *
 * The default result is:
 *
 * @code{.text}
 * RoModularWorkspace/
 * |-- .romodular-workspace
 * |-- AGENTS.md
 * |-- .codex/
 * |   `-- skills/
 * |-- .claude/
 * |   |-- CLAUDE.md
 * |   `-- skills/
 * |-- RoModular/
 * |-- RoModularAgents/
 * |-- RoModularBuild/
 * |-- Foundation/
 * |-- DspCore/
 * |-- MCC/
 * `-- MIDILAR/
 * @endcode
 *
 * **macOS:**
 *
 * @code{.sh}
 * ./scripts/bootstrap-workspace.sh
 * @endcode
 *
 * Preview the operation without writing files:
 *
 * @code{.sh}
 * ./scripts/bootstrap-workspace.sh \
 *   --root "$HOME/Developer/RoModularWorkspace" \
 *   --dry-run
 * @endcode
 *
 * **Windows PowerShell:**
 *
 * @code{.powershell}
 * ./scripts/bootstrap-workspace.ps1
 * @endcode
 *
 * Preview the Windows operation with `-DryRun`:
 *
 * @code{.powershell}
 * ./scripts/bootstrap-workspace.ps1 `
 *   -Root "$HOME/Code/RoModularWorkspace" `
 *   -DryRun
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section RoModularWorkspaceBootstrapBehavior Safe Existing-Checkout Behavior
 *
 * For every manifest entry, the scripts:
 *
 * 1. Clone a missing repository with its pinned Git submodules.
 * 2. Verify the `origin` URL when the directory already contains a Git
 *    worktree. The equivalent HTTPS forms with or without a trailing `.git`
 *    suffix are accepted.
 * 3. Leave every existing repository, branch, worktree, submodule, and
 *    uncommitted change untouched.
 * 4. Refuse a directory that is not a Git worktree or has an unexpected
 *    `origin`.
 *
 * The bootstrap never runs `pull`, `checkout`, `reset`, `clean`, merge, or
 * rebase. It is therefore safe to preview against an active development
 * workspace. A repository that requires synchronization remains an explicit
 * maintenance decision.
 *
 * @section RoModularWorkspaceBootstrapAgents Agent Configuration
 *
 * The script installs two provider adapters and two discovery views backed by
 * the same canonical instructions:
 *
 * - `AGENTS.md` at the workspace root is the Codex-compatible entry point.
 * - `.claude/CLAUDE.md` is the Claude Code entry point and imports the root
 *   `AGENTS.md` instead of duplicating its contents.
 * - `.codex/skills/` contains generated Codex-discoverable copies.
 * - `.claude/skills/` contains generated Claude-discoverable copies.
 *
 * Templates and skills are sourced from the cloned `RoModularAgents`
 * repository. The shared entry point loads its canonical contract and the
 * adapter belonging to each repository placed in scope.
 *
 * Existing workspace instructions are never overwritten silently. When a
 * different adapter already exists, the operation fails and preserves it.
 * `--force-config` on macOS or `-ForceConfig` on Windows is required to replace
 * either file or generated skill bundle deliberately. Canonical skills are
 * edited only under `RoModularAgents/skills/`.
 *
 * When the `codex` executable is available, the script prints the detected
 * version and the workspace launch command:
 *
 * @code{.sh}
 * codex -C "/path/to/RoModularWorkspace"
 * @endcode
 *
 * When `claude` is available, it prints the equivalent command launched from
 * the workspace root. Claude Code discovers `.claude/CLAUDE.md`, which uses
 * its supported `@path` import syntax to load `AGENTS.md`.
 *
 * The bootstrap does not install Codex or Claude Code, sign into either
 * service, modify user-level configuration, or store credentials. A missing
 * optional agent is reported without making repository setup fail.
 *
 * @section RoModularWorkspaceBootstrapOptions Options
 *
 * | macOS | Windows | Meaning |
 * | ----- | ------- | ------- |
 * | `--root <path>` | `-Root <path>` | Override the default `RoModularWorkspace` root |
 * | `--manifest <path>` | `-Manifest <path>` | Use an alternate repository manifest |
 * | `--force-config` | `-ForceConfig` | Replace differing workspace instructions and generated skills |
 * | `--dry-run` | `-DryRun` | Preview without filesystem changes |
 *
 * The `ROMODULAR_WORKSPACE_ROOT` environment variable supplies the root when
 * the corresponding command-line option is omitted.
 *
 * @section RoModularWorkspaceBootstrapArduino Arduino Libraries
 *
 * `scripts/install-arduino-libraries.sh` and
 * `scripts/install-arduino-libraries.ps1` clone the runtime libraries into an
 * Arduino libraries folder, using the origins from the same manifest:
 *
 * @code{.sh}
 * ./scripts/install-arduino-libraries.sh "$HOME/Documents/Arduino/libraries"
 * @endcode
 *
 * @code{.powershell}
 * ./scripts/install-arduino-libraries.ps1 "$HOME\Documents\Arduino\libraries"
 * @endcode
 *
 * CPSTL, Foundation, DspCore, MCC and MIDILAR are installed in dependency order at
 * the immutable tags in `.romodular/workspace/release-pins.txt`. Each library
 * is a Git clone named after its Arduino library. Running the script again
 * restores a clean clone to its declared tag; clones with local changes are
 * reported and left as they are. Any other existing folder is refused unless
 * `--force` or `-Force` replaces it. `--use-head` or `-UseHead` is the
 * explicit development opt-in: it tracks `main` and also includes unreleased
 * DspCore. `--include-legacy` and `-IncludeLegacy` are still accepted and
 * have no effect. `--dry-run` or `-DryRun` previews the operation. A sketch
 * includes a header of each library it uses, such as `<MCC.h>` or
 * `<MIDILAR_Devices.h>`. MCC and MIDILAR headers bring in the libraries they
 * depend on; with older releases, or with DspCore, the sketch also includes
 * `<Foundation.h>` and each dependency. CPSTL, Foundation, DspCore, MCC and
 * MIDILAR Arduino source builds support stock C++11 cores; CMake and direct
 * source integrations may have stricter requirements documented by their
 * owning repository.
 *
 * @section RoModularWorkspaceCli Read-Only Workspace CLI
 *
 * `scripts/romodular.sh` and `scripts/romodular.ps1` provide the same initial
 * host-side inspection commands for an existing workspace:
 *
 * @code{.sh}
 * ./scripts/romodular.sh doctor --root ..
 * ./scripts/romodular.sh status --root ..
 * ./scripts/romodular.sh sync --dry-run --root ..
 * @endcode
 *
 * The commands inspect local Git state and available host tools only. They do
 * not fetch, pull, check out, reset, clean, merge, clone, or build anything.
 * `sync --dry-run` is a plan-only command in this delivery. Repository-owned
 * scripts and CMake presets remain authoritative for compilation, tests,
 * packages, documentation, and MCU or board selection.
 *
 * @section RoModularWorkspaceBootstrapScan Project Scan
 *
 * `scripts/scan-project.py` reports which RoModular libraries and modules a
 * project or sketch uses, and suggests root headers to replace the umbrella
 * headers:
 *
 * @code{.sh}
 * python3 scripts/scan-project.py ../MIDILAR/examples/MIDILAR/Devices/TransposeThru
 * @endcode
 *
 * @code{.txt}
 * Suggested root headers:
 *   #include <MIDILAR_Devices.h>
 * @endcode
 *
 * The scan follows the project's own includes through the library sources and
 * reads the qualified names it uses, such as `MCC::Scales::Make`. Umbrella
 * headers such as `<MCC.h>` include every module, so they are not expanded.
 * The Arduino builder discovers a library only through a header at the root
 * of its `src` folder. When the suggested headers do not already bring in a
 * library that way, as with older releases of MCC and MIDILAR, the scan adds
 * one public header for it: the lightest module header the project already
 * uses, or the library's lightest module header when only its version is
 * needed. Internal headers such as `<Library_BuildSettings.h>` are never
 * suggested. The
 * libraries are looked up in the workspace that contains this checkout, or in
 * the folder given with `--libraries`, such as an Arduino libraries folder.
 *
 * The suggestion does not change the size of the program: unused code is
 * already discarded by the linker on every supported target. It shows what a
 * project depends on and avoids reading headers it does not need. The scan is
 * a static text analysis, so check the result by building the project.
 *
 * Unlike the bootstrap and installer, this optional tool is written in Python
 * 3 for both platforms instead of a shell and PowerShell pair.
 *
 * @section RoModularWorkspaceBootstrapReferences Agent Runtime References
 *
 * - <a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/tools-skills">OpenAI Agent Skills</a>
 * - <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills">Claude Code skills</a>
 * - <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/memory">Claude Code instruction imports</a>
 */
